WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
[melancholy music]
It looked like it was finally the end.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:07.900
This month-long campaign to keep me as the #1 subscriber

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.460
to keep me afloat, above the inevitable,

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:16.980
T-Series, a Sub Gap, was less than 15k yesterday.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.440
As closer than it's ever been. It looked like all hope, was lost.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.200
It looked like it was finally it. But then--

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.540
[dramatic music]
Something happened. Markiplier and Jacksepticeye--

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.640
finally showed up in the final hour, the last second.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.320
*laughing*
"I literally won't shut up until you subscribe to PewDiePie."

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.040
My friends who have previously been silent

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.260
for a mysterious unknown reasons,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.380
finally decided to extend their helping hand.

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:46.560
God bless you both.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.720
So yesterday we hit uh. 500--
*laughs*

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.380
500k subscribers. That's right.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.560
I definitely deserve this. Thank you very much,
*laughing*

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.180
You thought that was it, T-Series?

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.980
I bet--I bet you they were sitting there with champagne

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:06.620
ready to finally pop the bottle, "Ah geez, this has been obnoxious!"

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.020
"Ah, Jeez, this went on way longer than it should've."

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.400
NOT SO FAST T-SERIES! I don't think so!

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.140
There was a ton of other creators that showed their support as well and I--

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:19.560
seeing it all, it's just been amazing. All the fan support, all the memes--

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.900
I absolutely love it.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.720
I know I said, and I still mean it.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:26.460
I don't care if T-Series passes me, but this is all too fun.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.400
I don't remember the last time I had this much fun on YouTube.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.380
It just--everything has been insane.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.160
It all started with Mr. Beast creating the billboards to tell people to subscribe to me.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.620
Mr. Beast: "Ey! Uh, what's this one say again?"

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.220
Offscreen: "Subscribe to PewDiePie for original content"

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.760
Mr. Beast: "His content is SO original!"

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:48.700
Which then inspired my fans all across the world to do the same, hand out flyers, put up posters...

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:52.300
Justin Roberts bought the biggest billboard in New York City--
*laughing*

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:56.140
Justin: "IT'S THERE! OH MY GOD IT'S UP THERE."
Offscreen: "Oh! There it is!"

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.660
Justin: "We did it! We did it, it's up there!"

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.660
"Subscribe to PewDiePie right now guys!"

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:05.860
Davie504 played "B*tch Lasagna" for 10 hours straight!
*laughs*

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:14.560
[Davie504 playing B*tch Lasagna]

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:20.700
HackerGiraffe hacked 50k printers to tell people to subscribe to PewDiePie

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:26.120
Definitely a worthy cause. The amount of attention this is getting is just absolutely insane.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:32.400
Everyone seems so caught up, everyone seems so invested to this "subscribe to PewDiePie blah-blah-blah--."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.240
--and I honestly feel like I don't deserve it.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:39.240
I feel really weird about it, but it's a blast nonetheless.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.360
You've probably seen these live streams where it's PewDiePie vs. T-Series and uh--

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.200
Everyone is just so--invested into this.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.620
But there's a part of this that I really, really don't like

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.760
But--and it's a shame because I--

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.840
it is a vast majority of people,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.060
but at sometimes, in these comments--and you guys have told me this as well,

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:03.460
you see comments such as like, "F**k Indians" or "F**k Indians 'c-word'."

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:06.400
Just really distasteful, unnecessary comments.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.040
And I obviously made Indian jokes and stuff like that, but I do that of all countries and--

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.360
--this is is not what I'm about,

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.520
and I know my fan base isn't about this either.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.800
I'm getting more attention now that I'll probably ever get.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:22.820
And I feel really weird about it as well, so why not just take that fact and

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.320
redirect it to something more positive?

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.540
And show that this fan base, and this group of people can do something positive as well, because I know we can.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.360
No more, "F**k India."
Let's instead help India.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.060
Maybe you already knew this, or maybe you didn't,

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:41.420
but there's over 10 million child laborers in India between the age of 5 and 14,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.740
and even more between the age of 15 and 18.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:51.840
Almost 23 million. That means that almost 1 out of 10 kids in India are working.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.120
Now, this is mostly in rural areas,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:59.800
but this means that, a lot of kids in India are missing out-a chance for a proper education,

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.400
and a chance for a proper future.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:06.540
That's why I decided to create a fundraiser for the charity called "Cry."

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.900
"Cry" is a charity that focuses on making a better future for kids in India.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.060
The reason I picked "Cry" as a charity, is because

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.680
they recognize that just rescuing these kids won't be enough.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:21.040
So they instead work on identifying the root causes for these issues to solve them.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:26.560
Children, for example, work mainly to help their families, and because there's a high demand for child labor.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.280
But Cry setups strategies to prevent these issues,

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.020
and uproot them to build a better future for all of India.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:36.580
I think it's a great cause. I would highly encourage you to donate.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.840
I created a fundraiser down in the description.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.620
Please do check it out, and donate. Any bit will help.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:44.580
I will of course donate as well.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.840
And tomorrow between 4pm and 7pm UK time,

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.720
I will be live-streaming, where all the proceeds will go towards raising funds for this charity.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:57.260
Let's do something cool. I think we can turn this around and make it something really cool and really positive.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.560
Let's actually help 9-year-old kids in India. (Felix, we love you for what you are doing.♥️ ~India.)

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.340
That's it thank you for listening.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.000
Bye.

